codex
The direct `ValSeq` typing predicate confirms a limitation of this reference model: K does not refine a symbolic `Val` to the `Int` subsort from a recursive predicate. I’m switching the proof harness to an algebraic integer-list view (`IntSeq`) with the same two iterator equations as `list(vCons(...))`; this keeps induction typed and leaves the program body and all Python control semantics unchanged.
